From: NixOS Android devices contributors <nixos-android-devices@localhost>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 00:53:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] spmi: msm: encode one byte as a zero byte count

Local fix against U-Boot a06e89ab05eaa2b8344d521319399333cd760ae5:
https://source.denx.de/u-boot/u-boot/-/blob/a06e89ab05eaa2b8344d521319399333cd760ae5/drivers/spmi/spmi-msm.c

The SPMI arbiter command encodes length minus one. Both callbacks transfer
one byte, so byte count must be zero. The previous value one requests two
bytes and a write clears the adjacent register from the zero upper WDATA byte.

Reference: Linux v7.3-rc4 drivers/spmi/spmi-pmic-arb.c sets bc = len - 1:
https://git.kernel.org/pub/scm/linux/kernel/git/torvalds/linux.git/tree/drivers/spmi/spmi-pmic-arb.c?h=v7.3-rc4
On Asphalt this affects adjacent PMIC GPIO MODE/VIN/PULL registers and reboot
reason writes. The native test checks both command formatters.
---
--- a/drivers/spmi/spmi-msm.c
+++ b/drivers/spmi/spmi-msm.c
@@ -95,12 +95,12 @@
 
 static u32 pmic_arb_fmt_cmd_v1(u8 opc, u8 sid, u8 pid, u8 off)
 {
-	return (opc << 27) | (sid << 20) | (pid << 12) | (off << 4) | 1;
+	return (opc << 27) | (sid << 20) | (pid << 12) | (off << 4);
 }
 
 static u32 pmic_arb_fmt_cmd_v2(u8 opc, u8 off)
 {
-	return (opc << 27) | (off << 4) | 1;
+	return (opc << 27) | (off << 4);
 }
 
 static int msm_spmi_write(struct udevice *dev, int usid, int pid, int off,
